<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Routes for scenario_15 — scenario_14's five routes, translated for a cart that
  travels 6 m instead of 4 m. Lane is scenario_1's north-south lane (x=46.0) in
  the EBC area of patrick_henry_whole.

  A scenario JSON declares the scene/robot(asset)/assets/recording; the routes it can
  be driven along live here, one <route> per drive. Each route has a unique id so a
  scene script can pick which one to run (test_scene_1.py <scenario> <route_id>), and
  its own <start> pose (where the robot spawns for that route).

  Attributes:
    <route id="..."      unique route id within this scenario (required)
           leg_by_leg="true|false"  drive one NavigatePath per waypoint (pause
                                     between legs) vs one continuous path. Default true.
           description="..." >
    <start x="" y="" z=""       robot spawn pose for this route, map frame (meters,
           roll="" pitch="" yaw="" />  degrees). Required.
    <waypoint x="" y="" yaw=""  map-frame target (meters, degrees). Omit x or y for a
              roll="" pitch=""  rotation-only waypoint. yaw may be omitted (don't-care
              description="" /> arrival heading).

  TWO POINTS PER ROUTE: spawn, then one goal. No intermediate waypoints, so the
  whole path between them is the planner's to choose — which is the point.
  Anything the robot does around the cart is nav2's decision, not authored geometry.

  HOW THESE MAP ONTO scenario_14's FIVE ROUTES

  The 6 m trip parks the cart 2 m further north than scenario_14's 4 m trip, so
  every NORTH-side endpoint moves +2.0 m and every SOUTH-side endpoint stays put.
  That keeps each route's clearance to the cart identical to its scenario_14
  counterpart, so the two scenarios are comparable route-by-route.

    id   scenario_14        scenario_15        len 14 -> 15   character
     1   78.5 -> 85.5       78.5 -> 87.5       7.0 -> 9.0     northbound, tight both ends
     2   90.5 -> 80.5       92.5 -> 80.5      10.0 -> 12.0    southbound
     3   76.5 -> 86.5       76.5 -> 88.5      10.0 -> 12.0    northbound, long run-up
     4   90.5 -> 80.0       92.5 -> 80.0      10.5 -> 12.5    southbound, longer run-out
     5   78.0 -> 86.5       78.0 -> 88.5       8.5 -> 10.5    northbound, mid

  Reference extents used for the clearances:

    proxie                     1.03 m long -> 0.52 m from centre to either face
    cart at timeline t=0       y = 79.55..80.48   (where it sits when spawned)
    cart parked (t >= 12 s)    y = 85.55..86.48   (6 m north; was 83.55..84.48
                                                   in scenario_14's 4 m version)

  Route 1 is the tight case, derived the same way as scenario_14's route 1:
    south point  79.55 - 0.5 - 0.52 = 78.53  ->  y = 78.5
    north point  86.48 + 0.5 + 0.52 = 87.50  ->  y = 87.5
  The other four give the robot more room at one or both ends.

  Spawn clearance is checked against the cart's t=0 pose, not its parked pose: a
  run does Stop() -> Spawn -> Play(), and Stop() rewinds the timeline, so at the
  moment the robot is spawned the cart is still at its start. All five spawns are
  clear of BOTH cart positions.

  leg_by_leg is false throughout — with one waypoint it makes no practical
  difference, but it keeps each drive a single continuous NavigatePath.

  THE PASSING GEOMETRY IS DIFFERENT FROM scenario_14, NOT JUST LONGER

  6 m of travel carries the cart north of the Wall_29 pinch (x=47.65 over
  y=80.02..85.20). Measured against the PH greybox:

    scenario_14  cart parked y 83.55..84.48   east gap 1.35 m   west gap 9.30 m
    scenario_15  cart parked y 85.55..86.48   east gap 4.35 m   west gap 9.37 m

  scenario_14 effectively forces a west pass — its 1.35 m east gap is fully
  inflated at inflation_radius=0.75 from both the cart and the wall. Here the
  robot has 4.35 m to the east and a free choice of side. So if the two scenarios
  behave differently, trip length is not the only candidate explanation.

  The lane itself was checked clear over the whole span these routes use: no wall
  geometry intersects x=45.5..46.5 anywhere over y=72..95.

  WHAT THE ROBOT ACTUALLY MEETS: a PARKED cart, not a moving one. The cart's 12 s
  trip starts at Play(), and Apollo bringup outlasts it, so by the time the robot
  drives the cart has been sitting at y = 85.55..86.48 for a while. This is a
  static-obstacle test until the cart's time samples get a START HOLD (see the
  cart asset's header) or a proximity trigger.
-->
<routes scenario="scenario_15">

  <route id="1" leg_by_leg="false"
         description="Northbound, tight both ends: spawn 0.5 m south of the cart's start footprint and drive 9 m north to 0.5 m past its parked footprint at y=86. The minimum-clearance case - nav2 starts already on top of the obstacle with almost no run-up.">
    <start x="46.0" y="78.5" z="0.0" yaw="90.0" />
    <waypoint x="46.0" y="87.5" yaw="90.0" description="past_cart" />
  </route>

  <route id="2" leg_by_leg="false"
         description="Southbound: spawn 6 m north of the cart's parked footprint and drive 12 m south, finishing 2.5 m clear on the far side. The robot approaches the parked cart head-on with room to see it coming.">
    <start x="46.0" y="96.0" z="0.0" yaw="270.0" />
    <waypoint x="46.0" y="87.5" yaw="270.0" description="past_cart" />
  </route>

  <route id="3" leg_by_leg="false"
         description="Northbound with a long run-up: spawn 2 m further south than route 1 and finish 1 m further north, 12 m total, so the robot reaches the cart at a settled speed with a populated local costmap.">
    <start x="46.0" y="76.5" z="0.0" yaw="90.0" />
    <waypoint x="46.0" y="88.5" yaw="90.0" description="past_cart" />
  </route>

  <route id="4" leg_by_leg="false"
         description="Southbound with a longer run-out: as route 2 but finishing 0.5 m further south, 12.5 m total, giving more space to observe how the robot recovers the lane after passing.">
    <start x="46.0" y="95.0" z="0.0" yaw="270.0" />
    <waypoint x="46.0" y="87.5" yaw="270.0" description="past_cart" />
  </route>

  <route id="5" leg_by_leg="false"
         description="Northbound, mid: a half metre more run-up than route 1 and 1 m further past the cart, 10.5 m total. Sits between routes 1 and 3.">
    <start x="46.0" y="78.0" z="0.0" yaw="90.0" />
    <waypoint x="46.0" y="88.5" yaw="90.0" description="past_cart" />
  </route>

</routes>
